WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.468
How many?

2
00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:04.475
It is the most common question in any report.

3
00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:09.151
In this lesson, you will learn to write COUNT and DISTINCTCOUNT measures, show them

4
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:13.160
in cards, and choose the right one for your question. Let's count!

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.244
DAX is the formula language of Power BI.

6
00:00:18.244 --> 00:00:21.894
On this page, we compare two ways of counting.

7
00:00:21.894 --> 00:00:23.921
The first card uses COUNT:

8
00:00:23.921 --> 00:00:26.760
twenty two products, and twenty two categories.

9
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.400
Now a new measure:

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.650
Number of Products, Remove Duplicates.

11
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.800
It uses DISTINCTCOUNT on the Product column.

12
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.500
DISTINCTCOUNT counts each value only once.

13
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.642
I copy the card, paste it, and drop in the new measure.

14
00:00:56.642 --> 00:01:01.020
For products, we still get twenty two, because every product name is different.

15
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.093
Next:

16
00:01:41.093 --> 00:01:46.520
Number of Category, Remove Duplicates, using DISTINCTCOUNT on the Category column.

17
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.357
And now you can see the difference!

18
00:02:12.357 --> 00:02:15.902
COUNT gave twenty two categories, one for every row.

19
00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:19.840
DISTINCTCOUNT gives three, because there are only three unique categories.

20
00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.700
In the Format pane, I adjust the canvas, so every card has room.

21
00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.484
So remember:

22
00:02:45.484 --> 00:02:54.320
COUNT for every row, DISTINCTCOUNT for unique values, like the number of different sites, villages, or participants. Simple and powerful!

